secrets.json
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
state/corpus/

# The exam frames are working data, not the product. A user builds their own
# from their own product with build_generic.py --origin, so committing 76MB of
# somebody else's screenshots serves nobody — and these carry a real person's
# photograph, which is a thing a public repo should not do by accident.
golden/*/frames/
golden/*/sets/*/frames/

# The workbench stays on this machine. Studying another implementation as
# deeply as possible is required; shipping any part of it is not allowed —
# no import, no vendored tree, no artefact its trainer produced, and no
# runtime dependency that can change or disappear underneath us.
#
# `devtools/` holds the comparison harness and the corpus adapters. They are
# how "ours is better" got measured, and the measurement lives in the vault's
# Design Basis, never here.
devtools/
state/corpus/
state/corpus*/
state/*_corpus/

# Somebody else's benchmark. It is the external check this project leans on and
# it is not ours to redistribute — 8.2 MB of another group's dataset, vendored
# into a tree whose whole rule is that what ships is ours end to end. The audit
# already degrades gracefully when it is absent, so keeping it here on this
# machine costs nothing and shipping it was never a decision anyone made.
state/xroutebench/
